    "body": "Some thoughts after an internal chat:\r\n\r\nChrome's current model, where it changes the document across multiple history entries… the only other thing I'm aware of that does that is refresh.\r\n\r\nFirefox's current model, where it changes the document state of the current entry _only_, is more like `location.replace()`.",
